00:04:51,000 --> 00:04:57,000
Born leader.

2
00:09:42,000 --> 00:09:48,000
The Boss Baby is a animation, comedy, family film directed by Tom McGrath.

3
00:14:33,000 --> 00:14:39,000
A story about how a new baby's arrival impacts a family, told from the point of view of a
delightfully unreliable narrator, a wildly imaginative 7 year old named Tim.

4
00:19:24,000 --> 00:19:30,000
Theodore Templeton (voice), played by Alec Baldwin.

5
00:24:15,000 --> 00:24:21,000
Francis E. Francis (voice), played by Steve Buscemi.

6
00:29:06,000 --> 00:29:12,000
Tim Templeton (voice), played by Miles Bakshi.

7
00:33:57,000 --> 00:34:03,000
Ted Templeton (voice), played by Jimmy Kimmel.

8
00:38:48,000 --> 00:38:54,000
Janice Templeton (voice), played by Lisa Kudrow.

9
00:43:39,000 --> 00:43:45,000
Narrator / Older Tim Templeton (voice), played by Tobey Maguire.

10
00:48:30,000 --> 00:48:36,000
The Boss Baby is a 2017 American animated spy comedy film starring
Alec Baldwin as the voice of the titular character.

11
00:53:21,000 --> 00:53:27,000
Loosely based on the 2010 picture book The Boss Baby by Marla Frazee, it was
directed by Tom McGrath and written by Michael McCullers.

12
00:58:12,000 --> 00:58:18,000
Produced by DreamWorks Animation, it is the first
film in The Boss Baby franchise.

13
01:03:03,000 --> 01:03:09,000
The film follows a boy helping his baby brother who is a secret agent
in the war for adults' love between babies and puppies.

14
01:07:54,000 --> 01:08:00,000
The Boss Baby premiered at the Miami International Film Festival on March 12, 2017,
and was released in the United States on March 31 by 20th Century Fox.

15
01:12:45,000 --> 01:12:51,000
The film received mixed reviews from critics and was a commercial success,
grossing $528 million worldwide against a $125 million budget.

16
01:17:36,000 --> 01:17:42,000
The film was nominated for Best Animated Feature at the 90th
Academy Awards, the Annie Awards, and the Golden Globes.

17
01:22:27,000 --> 01:22:33,000
The success of the film spawned a franchise, including two television series, The Boss Baby: Back in
Business and The Boss Baby: Back In the Crib, and a sequel film, The Boss Baby: Family Business.

18
01:27:18,000 --> 01:27:24,000
The film explores themes of baby, villain, family
relationships, puppy, sibling rivalry.

19
01:32:09,000 --> 01:32:15,000
The tone is lighthearted.
